{"id": "EUVD-2026-59417", "enisaUuid": "a3b454cb-8e36-34a7-b20d-412693419535", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nhandshake: Require admin permission for DONE command\n\nACCEPT and DONE are the two downcalls of the handshake genl\nfamily, both intended for use by the trusted handshake agent\n(tlshd). ACCEPT already requires GENL_ADMIN_PERM; DONE has\nno privilege check at all.\n\nThe fd-lookup in handshake_nl_done_doit() only confirms that\nsome pending handshake request exists for the supplied sockfd;\nit does not authenticate the sender. An unprivileged process\nthat guesses or observes a valid sockfd can therefore submit\na DONE with HANDSHAKE_A_DONE_STATUS == 0, leaving the kernel\nconsumer to proceed as if the handshake succeeded. A non-zero\nstatus on a forged DONE tears down a legitimate in-flight\nhandshake before tlshd can report its real result.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:29", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/25fb53e43ec006ac69b9e825a7e8a11d63a6083e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6557f912509abe8e70223373dd7a44d1d4a0d6c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/67cec2f1eb9e58719d622e92e2278ceda72dbd85", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4dafc411948469277b276724c3b2b4408c02c04c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/81246a65303d9635266b1334490142caaf86a11f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fc6x-h5h8-wjr3", "CVE-2026-74270"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "60f451a1-9e12-39a7-b95a-63e784837c07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b3009ea8abb713b022d94fba95ec270cf6e7eae <4dafc411948469277b276724c3b2b4408c02c04c"}, {"id": "64bf9e32-e3d3-3490-8ff9-f77284567ac0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "73fb185c-1fe7-3c74-93c3-851fa64fa471", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "8728ee69-f868-323e-b783-fd0834a73501", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b3009ea8abb713b022d94fba95ec270cf6e7eae <67cec2f1eb9e58719d622e92e2278ceda72dbd85"}, {"id": "8d86e5f1-3653-3ce7-8399-0b1794ebea99", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "8ea9db8b-dc66-35b9-a545-6e06b6046f0f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "9196e581-75cf-3794-861c-090a869cd991", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a843e186-1cd9-35bf-9a91-c4c77d3b28a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b3009ea8abb713b022d94fba95ec270cf6e7eae <81246a65303d9635266b1334490142caaf86a11f"}, {"id": "ab10ac34-3e71-3a49-87f3-29fc0485209c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b3009ea8abb713b022d94fba95ec270cf6e7eae <b6557f912509abe8e70223373dd7a44d1d4a0d6c"}, {"id": "b321e58c-710a-3d64-918c-eba4f7d39fc0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4"}, {"id": "cc977f50-b76a-3a99-908a-b2581c1493c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "f5af1c4b-550c-3eac-b4bf-f0a793e613ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b3009ea8abb713b022d94fba95ec270cf6e7eae <25fb53e43ec006ac69b9e825a7e8a11d63a6083e"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c6362f55-001c-3272-b136-39b255c46709", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}